# These two tags exist to stop a package in the Debian archive from pointing
# apt somewhere else behind the administrator's back. This package is the
# base-files of a Debian derivative: shipping its own archive's source and the
# pin that keeps Debian's kernels out is exactly what it is for, and the
# alternative -- telling every user to write the files by hand -- is both worse
# and unauditable.
#
# The URL is visible in the package, the key is not shipped with it (see
# README.keyring), and removing this package removes both files again.
b1nix-base-files: package-installs-apt-sources [etc/apt/sources.list.d/b1nix.sources]
b1nix-base-files: package-installs-apt-preferences [etc/apt/preferences.d/b1nix-kernel]
